# Line endings, pinned.
#
# Why this file exists: with core.autocrlf=true and no attributes, git had guessed `server.mjs` as
# `-text` (see `git ls-files --eol`) and stored it with CRLF verbatim instead of normalising. Editing it
# with an LF-writing tool then flipped every line, so a ~60-line change committed as a 7367-line diff
# and the history stopped being reviewable. Pinning text files to LF in the repo fixes that for good.
#
# LF everywhere in the repo, regardless of what the working tree looks like on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Be explicit for what's actually tracked, so nothing is left to git's content guessing again.
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf

# Shell scripts MUST be LF or the shell refuses them. The pre-push hook is the gate that runs the whole
# test suite, so a CRLF here would silently disable it.
.githooks/*  text eol=lf
*.sh         text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never inspected, never converted. (The isometric office art is ~480 PNGs.)
*.png   binary
*.webp  binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db    binary
